      "titleImage": "https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=1hVRew1XR5qUySZt1FZl2Cnk1y7HHPoJ6",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "CONTINUITY AND CONTRASTS: ARCHITECTURAL EXPERIMENTS IN THE ALPINE VILLAGE OF SAVOGNO",
        "author": "fabio sciuchetti",
        "year": "Spring 2026",
        "tags": [
          "architecture",
          "model"
        ],
        "description": "The proposed projects do not stem from a mere formal intuition, but rather from a careful analysis of the village's needs and urban voids. Acknowledging the spatial fragmentation of the settlement, the chosen approach goes beyond simple restoration, aiming instead for a true adaptive reuse and functional conversion of the existing structures.<br><br>The goal is to trigger a chain reaction for the regeneration of the entire village through \"urban acupuncture\" interventions. Avoiding a massive, monolithic approach, the strategy is divided into four intervention lots, differing in typology and function, yet synergistically connected.<br><br>This subdivision also ensures the economic sustainability of the overall process, allowing for a phased development that can easily adapt to the client's actual financial resources.<br><br>Instagram Handles:<br>fabio sciuchetti @fabio_sciuchetti<br>",
        "course": "master thesis",
        "track": ", Laurea Magistrale, Y4"
      }
    }
